  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "rdsCnCEokWBImmt4iLTi8iIJHpc=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:24:39.575Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Kainos carries a major Workday practice \u2014 recorded in the workbook as Europe's largest boutique partner \u2014 alongside Microsoft and AWS credentials. The finding concerns what that practice is: Workday is an HR core rather than a workflow engine, so the tooling reveals no gap between what the platform does and what an attributed decision record would add.\n\nThe conclusion the research draws is deliberately narrow. The practice proves the firm can carry a major platform business, and nothing more. There is no identified missing record layer to point at, so there is no fit statement to make \u2014 only evidence of scale, which is not by itself a reason to approach anyone.\n\nThat is why the lead sits at 'do not pitch'. It is a screening outcome rather than a judgement on the firm, and writing it down prevents the Workday credential from being mistaken later for evidence of workflow relevance simply because it is a large enterprise platform.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Kainos (UK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> HR core, not workflow. Proves the firm carries a major platform practice, nothing more.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:24:39.575115Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:24:39.575119Z"
    }
  },
